Fixed the bug in `src/url_utils.ts`. The `normalizeUrl` function had a `break` statement inside the tracking-parameter loop, so it only stripped the first matching parameter and stopped. Removing `break` lets all parameters in `TRACKING_PARAMS` get stripped.

Verified with a test covering URLs containing multiple tracking params (e.g. `utm_source` + `fbclid`, and `utm_source` + `utm_medium` + `utm_campaign`) — all now normalize to the clean URL.


